PHILLIP ISOLA: Great.

5
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:16,360
So welcome.

6
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:19,680
This lecture is going to be on generalization.

7
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,240
So this is the next topic in the series of how

8
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:23,580
do you approximate functions?

9
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:26,040
Now do they actually generalize?

10
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:30,180
And the basic question is, do neural networks generalize?

11
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:33,220
And well, we'll see, yes, the answer is yes to some degree.

12
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:34,780
And then the question is why?

13
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:36,020
Why do they generalize?

14
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,940
A few logistical reminders.

15
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:43,240
Problem set one is due today.

16
